<section class="section reveal" id="linear-algebra-foundations">
  <span class="section-label">Fundamentals</span>
  <h2>Linear Algebra Foundations for AI</h2>

  <p>Linear algebra is not just mathematics—it is the language in which machine learning operates. Every neural network layer performs matrix multiplications. Every regression model uses matrix inversion. Every dimensionality reduction technique exploits properties of vectors and matrices. To be effective in AI, you need to understand linear algebra deeply enough to see through the abstractions and debug when things go wrong.</p>

  <p>In this lesson, we focus on the operations you will encounter most frequently in production AI systems. We do not dive into theoretical proofs, but we explain the intuition behind each operation so you can understand when to use it and what can go wrong.</p>

  <div class="analogy">
    <h4>💡 Think of It This Way</h4>
    <p>Vectors are directions and magnitudes in space. Matrices are transformations that rotate, scale, or shear space. Matrix multiplication chains transformations together. Understanding linear algebra is understanding how transformations compose and interact—crucial knowledge for designing and debugging AI systems.</p>
  </div>

